# Cursor & IDE Agent Rules for `angband3d`

Before starting any task, read `AGENTS.md` (Turn-0 Master Operating Manual) and `docs/STATE.md`.

## 1. Orientation Order
1. `git status -s`
2. `docs/STATE.md` (active checklist & gate log; `docs/NEXT_STEPS.md` is history only)
3. `docs/plan/EXECUTOR_START_HERE.md` & `docs/plan/master_audit_and_execution_plan.md` (Part VI: Atomic Execution Cards 1–5 & 8 Golden Anti-Trap Guardrails)
4. `docs/LLM_CONTEXT.md`, `docs/PROTOCOL.md`, and `docs/BEST_PRACTICES_AND_LESSONS_LEARNED.md`

## 2. Verification Gates
- Fast Gate (run after every edit): `node tools/run_tests.js --tier fast`
- Native Bridge Smoke Gate: `python tools/smoke_test.py` (11/11)
- C# Build Gate: `dotnet build client/angband3d.csproj` && `dotnet build desktop/Angband3D.csproj`
- Asset Version & Android Sync (after any `server/public/` change): `node tools/bump_version.js && npm run android:sync`

## 3. Non-Negotiable Invariants (`L1–L34`)
- Never run unbounded `**/*` searches or dump full multi-thousand-line files; use line-bounded reads and surgical replacements.
- Before adding/editing a method in a large class (`dungeon3d.js`, `app.js`, `hud.js`, `terminal.js`, `chronicle-*.js`), search the file for duplicate method definitions (`L23`).
- Engine changes stay strictly in `main-bridge.c/.cpp` and `bridge-json.c/.h`. Export patch with `--output=`. Guard grid access with `bridge_in_play()` and equipment with `bridge_get_equipped_by_type()`.
- Movement = arrow keys (`up`/`down`/`left`/`right`); Hold = `,`. Never send raw digits (`0`–`9`) for movement/hold (`L2`); never write `sendKey('5')` in `input.js`.
- `-more-` prompts during `play` (`overlay == 0`) stay in 3D view with the HUD message banner (`L16`).
- Escape all dynamic strings rendered via `innerHTML` with `escapeHtml()`.
- Gate all per-frame DOM, Canvas2D, and 3D `InstancedMesh`/`MultiMesh` updates on state-change signatures (`L25`), and explicitly `.dispose()` removed GPU/audio resources (`L26`).
